course: dictionary
lesson: 14312
title: Reading an obituary
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An obituary is a piece of writing in a newspaper or on a website, printed after someone has died. It tells the reader about that person's life and what they did. «The newspaper printed an obituary of the famous footballer, with photos of his best goals.» The word tells you a person has died, and the rest of the text tells you about their life.
explain: Obituaries are non-fiction, which means they are true and about real people. They are written in a polite, formal style, so they are calm and respectful, even when the writer feels sad. «Mum helped my cousin write an obituary for our gran, who taught music for forty years.» Notice the careful, kind words.
explain: You will hear the word in different ways. «Every morning, Dad reads the obituaries to see who has died in our town.» Here obituaries means many pieces of writing. In everyday talk, some people also use obituary for a short notice that someone has died, without the full story of their life.
fact: An obituary is a piece of writing about a person's life, printed after they have died.
fact: Obituaries appear in newspapers and on websites.
fact: Obituaries are non-fiction, so they are true stories about real people.
fact: Obituaries are written in a polite, formal style, even when the writer is sad.
fact: In everyday talk, an obituary can also be a short notice that someone has died.
exercise: «The newspaper printed an obituary of the famous footballer.» What is an obituary? | A letter sent to a friend on their birthday | A story about a made-up dragon | *A piece of writing about someone's life, printed after they have died | A list of the football results for the week
exercise: «Ella's family wrote an obituary about her gran, who was a nurse.» What did the obituary tell readers? | A recipe for her favourite cake | *What her gran did in her life, and that she had died | The weather on her birthday | How to play the piano
exercise: «The obituary was sad to share that Mr Patel had died last Tuesday.» Which word tells you the person is no longer alive? | obituary | Tuesday | *died | sad
test: What kind of text is an obituary? | Fiction, a made-up story | A poem with rhyming lines | *Non-fiction, a true text about a real life | A joke book
test: What style is an obituary usually written in? | Loud and silly, with lots of jokes | Whispered and secret | Rude and angry | *A polite, formal style
exam: «The obituary said Mrs Wood had lived a long life of gardening.» What is the main job of an obituary? | To sell new gardening tools | To ask readers for money | *To tell readers about a person's life and that they have died | To tell a funny joke
